gcc-spe: SPU nop with a register operand in the assembler's syntax

The nopn pattern prints its operand as a bare number, "nop 127", which
older gas read as register 127. binutils 2.47 assembles it as 127 bytes
of nop padding (32 instructions), so the nops spu_emit_branch_hint() puts
between a close hint and its branch push the branch out of the hint's
reach:

  Error: Relocation doesn't fit. (relocation value = 0x414)

Print the operand as a register, "nop $127", a single instruction.

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

--- a/gcc/config/spu/spu.md
+++ b/gcc/config/spu/spu.md
@@ -4437,7 +4437,7 @@ selb\t%0,%4,%0,%3"
 (define_insn "nopn"
   [(unspec_volatile [(match_operand:SI 0 "immediate_operand" "K")] UNSPECV_NOP)]
   ""
-  "nop\t%0"
+  "nop\t$%0"
   [(set_attr "type" "nop")])
 
 (define_insn "lnop"
